<title>USA: CapStar buys two hotels for $47.5 mln.</title>
<headline>CapStar buys two hotels for $47.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>CapStar Hotel Co said Wednesday it has completed the purchase of a hotel in Houston and another in Albuquerque, N.M., for $47.5 million.</p>
<p>It said the hotels it bought are the 295-room Westchase Hilton in Houston, from the Redstone Group, and the 294-room Doubletree Hotel in Albuquerque, from Mervin Griffin Hotels.</p>
<p>Paul Whetsell, CapStar's chairman and chief executive officer, said his company continues to aggressively seek similar, well-positioned properties to add to its portfolio.</p>
</text>
